menu "Example Configuration"

    config ENABLE_MEMORY_PROFILING
        bool "Enable Memory Profiling"
        default n
        help
            Enable this option to include memory profiling features in the example.
            This will allow you to monitor memory usage during runtime.

endmenu

menu "Debugging"
    config BLE_SHELL_DEBUGGING_ENCRYPTED
        bool "Enable BLE shell debugging (encrypted)"
        default n
        help
          Adds a BLE UART-style console service that requires LE pairing.

    config BLE_CONSOLE_REQUIRE_BOND
        bool "Require bonded peer (not just encrypted) for BLE console"
        default y
        depends on BLE_SHELL_DEBUGGING_ENCRYPTED
        help
          When enabled (default), the console rejects access unless the peer
          is both encrypted AND bonded. If disabled, encrypted-but-unbonded
          peers are allowed.

    config BLE_CONSOLE_RATE_LIMIT
        bool "Enable TX rate limiter for BLE console notifications"
        default y
        depends on BLE_SHELL_DEBUGGING_ENCRYPTED
        help
          When enabled (default), outgoing notify traffic is throttled to
          avoid starving Matter/NimBLE. Tuned conservatively for ESP32-C3.
endmenu

